<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  Namer_BlackstarCompany.xml                Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-23
  ============================================================================

  BLACKSTAR_NAMES_EVERY_PIRATE_1. Owner's ruling 2026-08-23: "Fix it properly."

  🔴 WHY THE NAME MOVED OFF `fixedName`. `Pirate` is ALSO `PirateBandBase` - vanilla
  gives it a Name= attribute as well as a defName, so it is simultaneously a concrete
  faction and the abstract parent of every other pirate. Anything added to it is
  inherited, so a single `fixedName` made SIX factions call themselves Blackstar
  Company: Pirate, CannibalPirate, PirateYttakin, PirateWaster, DV_PirateKeshig and
  AG_XenohumanPirates.

  ⛔ TWO OBVIOUS FIXES DO NOT WORK, and both were ruled out from the ENGINE SOURCE:
     - Blanking the child with <fixedName></fixedName> resolves to the EMPTY STRING,
       because XmlInheritance.RecursiveNodeCopyOverwriteElements strips the parent's
       text when the child node has no content. FactionGenerator.cs:149 then reads
       `if (factionDef.fixedName != null)` - a NULL test, not NullOrEmpty - so the
       faction would be named "". Five factions called nothing is worse than five
       called Blackstar.
     - Inherit="False" only clears CHILD ELEMENTS of the node it sits on. It cannot
       un-inherit a scalar from the parent.

  ✅ SO THE NAME COMES FROM A NAMER INSTEAD. `factionNameMaker` is ALSO inherited, but
  unlike fixedName it can be overridden per child with a real value - and three of the
  five already override it with their own namers (NamerFactionPirateYttakin,
  NamerFactionPirateWaster, DV_NamerFactionPirateKeshig). Only CannibalPirate and
  AG_XenohumanPirates inherit NamerFactionPirate, and BlackstarCompany.xml now pins
  those two back to vanilla explicitly.

  🔑 A one-rule pack always produces the same string, so this is a fixed name in
  everything but mechanism - and the mechanism is the point, because it is overridable.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <RulePackDef>
    <defName>Jawa_NamerFactionBlackstar</defName>
    <rulePack>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>r_name->Blackstar Company</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </rulePack>
  </RulePackDef>

</Defs>
